<main><div class="eyebrow">JobStamp</div><h1>Delete account &amp; data</h1><p class="lead">This page explains how to delete your JobStamp user account and the personal account data associated with it.</p>
<section><h2>Delete your account directly in JobStamp</h2><p>If you still have access to the app, you can initiate deletion directly within JobStamp.</p><div class="box"><ol><li>Open JobStamp.</li><li>Open Settings.</li><li>Go to your user account section.</li><li>Select <strong>“Delete account”</strong>.</li><li>Confirm deletion as described in the app.</li></ol></div></section>
<section><h2>Request deletion without access to the app</h2><p>If you can no longer use JobStamp or have already uninstalled the app, you can request deletion of your account by email.</p><div class="box important"><p><strong><a href="mailto:pabaapps@web.de?subject=JobStamp%20-%20Account%20deletion">pabaapps@web.de</a></strong></p><p>If possible, use the email address registered with your JobStamp account.</p></div></section>
<section><h2>What is removed when an account is deleted?</h2><ul><li>the JobStamp sign-in account,</li><li>the personal assignment to companies,</li><li>the link between the user account and an employee profile,</li><li>personal profile data such as name and email address where no longer required,</li><li>personally assigned feedback and active personal timer data.</li></ul><p>Individual technical or historical records may be anonymised so they can no longer be linked to the deleted user account.</p></section>
<section><h2>Business data</h2><p>Data that forms part of a company's business documentation is not automatically deleted when an individual user account is deleted. This may include, for example, jobs, work-time records, material bookings or other company data. The personal user link is removed.</p></section>
<section><h2>Special case for company owners</h2><p>If the account to be deleted is the last owner of a company, a decision must first be made about the company.</p><ul><li>Ownership can be transferred to another linked user account.</li><li>Alternatively, the company and its associated company data can be permanently deleted.</li></ul></section>
<section><h2>Deletion of a company</h2><p>If a company is permanently deleted in JobStamp, the associated company data is removed from the JobStamp cloud. This includes in particular customers, jobs, work-time data, material data, team assignments and other data assigned to the company.</p><p>The personal user accounts of other team members are not automatically deleted.</p></section>
<section><h2>Retention obligations</h2><p>Where statutory obligations or other legal grounds require certain data to be retained, such data may be stored for the required period. In that case, it will be processed only for the relevant retention purpose and deleted once the retention ground no longer applies.</p></section>
